  "2026-06-25T04:57:09.804Z",codex-pm-ecosystem-audit-20260625,"Duplicate check: status-all searches for terminal resolution metadata backfill and active planning metadata found closed governance tooling items pm-yq7m, pm-fryg, pm-wbak-class work, and pm-6bz1, but no open execution item for historical backfill."
  "2026-07-04T20:56:40.819Z",codex-agent,"Audit evidence 2026-07-04 continuation: pm validate --check-resolution --check-history-drift --json is ok:true for history_drift across 1506 checked items and warns only validate_resolution_missing_fields:268 across closed historical items. This confirms pm-e9zh remains the canonical open remediation for terminal resolution/expected/actual backfill; no duplicate item created. The earlier list --filter-resolution-missing projection showed 198 closed rows because it counts a narrower filter than validate resolution details. Keep the existing no-placeholder and changelog-drag rules."
  "2026-07-05T05:51:00.468Z",claude-code-agent,"Live validation handoff from pm-lodl/pm-8778 lane: pm validate --check-resolution --check-history-drift --json on 2026-07-05 returned ok:true with history_drift ok across 1536 checked items and the pre-existing validate_resolution_missing_fields:268 warning. This confirms pm-e9zh remains the canonical open remediation for historical terminal resolution metadata; no duplicate item created from this lane."
  "2026-07-07T14:41:49.016Z",maintainer-agent,"2026-07-07 verification: validate_resolution_missing_fields now 269 (body says 268; +1 from a recently closed item missing structured resolution) and missing_close_reason steady at 18. Reinforces the DoD: new closes must always carry -m/-r/-d so this count never grows."
  "2026-07-07T15:15:38.523Z",maintainer-agent,"2026-07-07 verification (planning pass, later same day): validate_resolution_missing_fields steady at 269 and missing_close_reason steady at 18 — no drift since the previous pass. New closes continue to carry structured resolution per the DoD."
  "2026-07-13T21:41:33.985Z",codex-root,"Validation refresh 2026-07-13: pm validate --check-resolution --check-history-drift remains structurally healthy with zero history drift, but reports validate_resolution_missing_fields:276 terminal records. This is the canonical debt item; do not create placeholder values or broad duplicate cleanup work. Preserve historical meaning, wait for the pm-wrbe policy dependency, then repair in a dedicated evidence-backed pass with changelog and validation proof at the true end state."
  "2026-07-21T07:57:07.653Z",codex-root-20260721,"2026-07-21 shipping-lane verification: pm validate reports 276 closed items missing one or more structured resolution fields and zero history drift. The count is unchanged from the latest recorded baseline, so this canonical evidence-backed backfill item remains open; no placeholders or duplicate cleanup item were introduced."
  "2026-07-24T12:09:37.095Z",claude-code-agent,"Current validation evidence: pm validate --check-resolution --check-history-drift is ok with zero drift across 1,929 current items and reports 287 historical terminal records missing one or more structured resolution fields. This remains the canonical evidence-preserving backfill owner; no placeholders or duplicate cleanup item were introduced."
  "2026-07-26T17:17:15.948Z","harness:claude-code","Unblocked 2026-07-26. The constraint that held this item was that a metadata write on a long-closed item re-buckets it into the current changelog section, because attribution resolved through closed_at ?? updated_at ?? created_at and 1,488 of 1,795 terminal items carried no closed_at. That is no longer true.\n\nEvery terminal item now carries a release identifier derived from the tag whose window contains its close event, taken from its immutable history stream: 1,782 stamped, 13 deliberately left unstamped because they close after the newest tag and therefore belong to the pending window. The derivation was validated against ground truth before any write — for the 307 items that already had closed_at, the history-derived instant matched on 307 and disagreed on 0.\n\nThe generator honours the release field as the attribution authority under --all-release-tags, which was proved directly rather than assumed: stamping a closed item, which moved its updated_at to now, produced a byte-identical CHANGELOG.md. After the full backfill, regeneration moved 295 items and every one of those moves matched the derivation, with no items added or removed and the Unreleased section unchanged.\n\nThe practical consequence for this item: the backfill work it describes can now proceed as ordinary mutations without changelog churn, and the ordering constraint that deferred it no longer applies. Evidence and method are recorded on pm-3j6it6.\n"
  "2026-07-27T23:34:12.968Z","harness:codex","2026-07-27 broad SDK/CLI shipping-lane refresh: pm validate --check-resolution --check-history-drift is ok with zero history drift across 2,144 current items and reports 291 historical terminal records missing one or more structured resolution fields. The seven items closed in this lane all carry evidence-backed resolution/expected/actual fields, so this debt did not grow from current work. pm-e9zh remains the canonical dedicated backfill owner; no placeholders, duplicate item, or unrelated bulk mutation was introduced."
  "2026-07-28T22:39:25.096Z","harness:claude-code","Live count 2026-07-28: pm validate --check-resolution reports 291 closed items missing structured resolution evidence across 1,855 closed items, and it remains the only validate warning class still raised on this workspace - every other class this project has tracked is now clear. The remediation hints the check emits name resolution, expected_result and actual_result per item, so the worklist is fully enumerated and machine-readable. Recording the count so the trend is visible from the item rather than from a run log; no placeholder text was written, per this item's own constraint.\n"
  "2026-07-29T21:26:21.227Z","harness:codex","Live validation evidence 2026-07-29: pm validate --check-resolution --check-history-drift checked all 2,197 items, found zero history drift, zero missing or unreadable streams, zero hash mismatches, and zero chain mismatches. The only validation warning class is 292 terminal items missing structured resolution metadata. This item remains the canonical owner; placeholder backfills are explicitly not acceptable."
  "2026-07-31T14:27:39.500Z","harness:claude-code","Current count 2026-07-31: pm validate --check-resolution reports validate_resolution_missing_fields:292 across the corpus, over 2,231 items of which 1,900 are closed. The remediation hints the validator emits are placeholder-shaped ('Describe how this item was resolved'), which is exactly the shape this chore exists to avoid, so the count should not be reduced by accepting them. History drift is clean at 0 drifted items over 2,231 checked streams, so every one of the 292 has an intact stream from which real resolution evidence can be reconstructed rather than invented - the close_reason and the closing comments are in the record even where the structured fields are empty."
  "2026-08-02T18:18:40.421Z","harness:codex","Live validation evidence 2026-08-02: pm validate --check-resolution --check-history-drift checked all 2,278 items with zero missing/unreadable streams, zero hash or chain mismatches, and zero history drift. It reports 295 historical terminal items missing one or more resolution/expected_result/actual_result fields. The two items closed in the current SDK/CLI tranche were immediately completed with evidence-backed structured fields and are not part of that residual. This canonical chore remains open and unclaimed; no placeholder backfill or duplicate cleanup item was created."
  "2026-08-07T19:48:53.302Z","harness:codex","Live validation evidence 2026-08-07: pm validate --check-resolution --check-history-drift checked all 2368 items with zero missing/unreadable streams, zero hash or chain mismatches, and zero history drift. The only warning remains 295 historical terminal items missing structured resolution fields, unchanged from the 2026-08-02 baseline. Current tranche closes carry evidence-backed fields; no placeholders, bulk normalize mutation, or duplicate cleanup item was introduced."
  "2026-08-18T16:34:51.331Z","harness:codex","Live validation refresh 2026-08-18: strict unbounded pm validate checked 2,522 items with zero missing/unreadable streams, zero hash or chain mismatches, and zero history drift. The only warning remains 295 historical terminal items missing structured resolution fields, unchanged from the 2026-08-02 and 2026-08-07 baselines. Current SDK/CLI tranche items carry evidence-backed resolution fields; no placeholders, bulk backfill, or duplicate item was introduced."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-04T18:50:14.133Z",maintainer-agent,"Scope addition from 2026-07-04 backlog audit (pm-y904): duplicate issue-code pair GH-209 (pm-1byt canonical, pm-25se follow-up) involves two CLOSED items, so per the changelog updated_at invariant it must be resolved in this careful backfill pass (set duplicate_of on pm-25se or retitle) together with the changelog regen, not in a create-only audit."
  "2026-07-06T13:13:56.245Z",maintainer-agent,"Audit #10 2026-07-06: validate_resolution_missing_fields grew 268 -> 269. The new entry is ADR pm-muhw (accepted+closed 2026-07-05 without resolution/expected_result/actual_result). Do NOT touch it now (changelog drag — it sits in the shipped 2026.7.6 bucket); fold it into this dedicated backfill pass. Real evidence exists: acceptance rationale is in its comments and the SDK-first epic pm-usfg body."
body: "## Context\npm validate reports validate_resolution_missing_fields:268 and validate_metadata_missing_close_reason:18 — historical terminal items closed before the structured-resolution era (resolution/expected_result/actual_result via pm update, close -m/-r/-d from PR#230) lack that evidence.\n\n## Rules of engagement\n- NO placeholders: only backfill where real evidence exists (item history, linked PR/commit, session memory, CHANGELOG entry). An honest empty beats \"done: done\".\n- Changelog drag trap: touching CLOSED items updates updated_at, which pm-changelog uses for release bucketing — a bulk backfill would drag old items into the current [Unreleased]. Do the backfill in a dedicated tracker-only pass where the changelog is regenerated and reviewed in the same commit (same protocol as pm-pivf), or teach pm-changelog to bucket by closed_at first.\n- Work oldest→newest in small batches; record per-batch counts (missing_fields before/after) as comments here.\n\n## Definition of done\nvalidate_resolution_missing_fields reduced to only items with genuinely unrecoverable evidence (documented count); missing_close_reason:18 → 0; no unintended [Unreleased] churn in the same commit's regenerated changelog."
